@startuml
title Bonecutters Hosted Boundary
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Owner" as Owner
component "Bonecutters deploy role" as DeployRole
component "Bonecutters provisioning access" as Provisioning
component "client/dist" as Dist
cloud "Bonecutters private S3 bucket\nREST origin" as S3
component "CloudFront OAC" as OAC
cloud "Bonecutters CloudFront distribution" as CloudFront
component "ACM certificate\nus-east-1" as Certificate
cloud "www.bonecutters.us" as Www
cloud "bonecutters.us" as Root
cloud "simpleetl.bonecutters.us" as SimpleEtl

Owner --> Provisioning : human-approved setup
Owner --> DeployRole : assumes project-scoped deploy access
DeployRole --> S3 : publish static assets
DeployRole --> CloudFront : invalidate cache
Dist --> S3 : uploaded build output
CloudFront --> OAC : signs origin requests
OAC --> S3 : private origin access
Certificate --> CloudFront : viewer TLS
Www --> CloudFront : canonical site
Root --> CloudFront : redirect to www

note right of SimpleEtl
SimpleETL remains a separate subdomain,
deployment boundary, and resource set.
Bonecutters deployment must not reuse or
mutate SimpleETL resources.
end note

@enduml
